WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:06.220
2018 was a pretty rotten year
for stock market investors.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.450
It's been a fairly long
bull market in America,

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.440
really, since March 2009.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.810
What I mean by bull market is share prices

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.830
have risen pretty steadily
without a very big setback,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.760
so share prices in America have raced

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.500
away from pretty much everywhere else.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.760
From Europe, from Japan,
from emerging markets.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.280
America's really been the place

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.200
where stock market
investors have wanted to be.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.393
The questions is, is that
gonna be true in 2019?

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.840
In a market that's
coming pretty mature now,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.080
going into it's 10th year,

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.870
is there really very much
upside from US stocks anymore?

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.610
You might want to start
looking somewhere else,

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.530
looking at Europe, looking
at emerging markets

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.900
which haven't been rising quite as quickly

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.530
and, therefore, are cheaper
and of better value.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.210
The other way of looking
at things is to say,

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.960
if things are getting risky,
after a pretty awful year

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.660
like 2018, I might just
want to double down

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.950
on the things that have
done well for me so far.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:04.780
Stick with America, stick
with technology stocks,

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:05.960
so-called FAANG.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.280
That's Facebook, Apple,
Amazon, Netflix, and Google.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.340
These are the companies
that investors think

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.520
are gonna do well, not just
for the next few years,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.240
but for the next few decades.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.600
The problem with that view is,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.900
it does rely on the US economy continuing

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.330
to do better than economies elsewhere.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.140
Most people think next
year will be a slower year

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.973
for US economic growth.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.110
China's economy has
actually been slowing down,

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:36.420
and that's not just because
of Donald Trump's trade war.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.130
There's also been an underlying slowdown

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.730
in consumer spending
in the Chinese economy,

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.270
and that hasn't just affected China.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.990
That's affected all the local
emerging markets in Asia

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.810
and it's also affected Europe.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.910
About a third of the profits that European

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:52.270
listed companies make
come either from China

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.820
or from other emerging markets
that are tied into China.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.640
So when China slows, Europe slows as well.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.330
The Chinese government is worried

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:01.820
about the degree to which
the economy has been slowing,

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.460
so it's been trying to gee
up the economy a little bit

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.470
by cutting taxes, by
relaxing monitoring policy,

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.200
and by spending more on infrastructure.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.640
If that starts to percolate through

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.660
into the Chinese economy next year,

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.560
you could also see growth picking up

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.450
in economies that rely
heavily on Chinese demand

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.473
in Asia but also in Europe.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.040
Half of investors think it's best to stick

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.550
with the US market, and
half of investors think

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.640
it will be better to look
elsewhere for growth.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.300
We're looking forward here
and we don't really know

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.010
what's gonna happen in 2019.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.360
Investors always have to
deal with uncertainty.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.660
What's the best way to deal with that?

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.020
Well, in general, it makes sense

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.040
to try and spread your bets widely,

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.770
not to put all your eggs in one basket

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:46.600
as investors have been doing
with the American market.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.970
Buy a basket of stocks
that gives you exposure

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.270
to a wide range of emerging markets,

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.220
and also a basket of stocks
that gives you exposure

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.840
to a lot of rich
economies outside America.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.580
That's Europe and Japan and Australia.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.503
Spread your bets is probably
the best strategy for 2019.

